@lang en
IMPORT `bvvcx-claim`

-- Evidence for the findings in NOTES.md §4 (the hostile reading). Each assertion here PASSES:
-- it shows the encoding giving the surprising answer the text, read as the fork register
-- reads it, produces. The finding number is on each block.

§ `Findings — evidence`

§§ `X1 — "the driver" is defined by consent, so exclusions about the driver miss a thief`

GIVEN `consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A claim`
`a collision by a driver at 80 mg of alcohol, consent:` `consent` MEANS
    `a standard claim under` `the standard policy` `for` `the standard collision` `,` `the driving`
    WHERE
        `the driving` MEANS
            `driven by` (`a person driving: consent` `consent` `, licence` FALSE `, expired` FALSE `, right class` FALSE `, withdrawn` FALSE `, learner` FALSE `, blood` (JUST 80) `, breath` NOTHING `, drugs` FALSE `, refused a test` FALSE) `,` `careful driving`

-- The owner's friend, drunk and unlicensed: excluded twice over. A thief in the same state: paid.
#ASSERT `the cover decision for` (`a collision by a driver at 80 mg of alcohol, consent:` TRUE) EQUALS `excluded by` (LIST `11.3 no proper driving licence`, `11.4 alcohol or drugs`)
#ASSERT `the amount payable on` (`a collision by a driver at 80 mg of alcohol, consent:` FALSE) EQUALS 16_000_000

§§ `X2 — the exclusions ask for no causal link: hail on a parked car with a lapsed inspection certificate`

`hail on a parked car whose inspection certificate has lapsed` MEANS
    `a standard claim under` `the standard policy` `for` `the event` `,` `nobody driving`
    WHERE
        `the event` MEANS
            `an event on` (YMD 2026 6 15) `: peril` `a natural catastrophe beyond human control` `, sudden` TRUE `, at` `in Vietnam` `, war` FALSE `, deliberate` EMPTY
                `, hired out` FALSE `, inspection` (`inspection: valid` FALSE `, new and awaiting inspection` FALSE `, circulating temporarily` FALSE) `, load` `a normal load` `, parts` `the standard parts`
                `, paint` NOTHING `, police suspension` FALSE `, earlier part thefts` 0

#ASSERT `the cover decision for` `hail on a parked car whose inspection certificate has lapsed` EQUALS `excluded by` (LIST `11.2 no valid inspection certificate`)
#ASSERT `the amount payable on` `hail on a parked car whose inspection certificate has lapsed` EQUALS 0

§§ `X3 — a theft reported in 20 hours meets 5.2.10's 24 hours and still loses 10% under 15.1.1(a)`

`a stolen car reported after 20 hours` MEANS
    `a claim: vehicle` `the standard vehicle` `, policy` `the standard policy` `, claimant` `the insured named on the certificate`
        `, event` `the event` `, driving` `nobody driving`
        `, conduct` (`conduct: told after hours` (JUST 20) `, written notice after days` (JUST 2) `, force majeure` FALSE `, moved without consent` FALSE `, for safety` FALSE `, repaired without consent` FALSE `, dishonest` FALSE `, 15.1.3 rate` NOTHING)
        `, shortfall` `no premium shortfall` `, costs` `no costs` `, hire` NOTHING `, wreck` `no wreck kept` `, other insurance` EMPTY
    WHERE
        `the event` MEANS
            `an event on` (YMD 2026 6 15) `: peril` `theft of the whole vehicle` `, sudden` TRUE `, at` `in Vietnam` `, war` FALSE `, deliberate` EMPTY
                `, hired out` FALSE `, inspection` `a valid inspection certificate` `, load` `a normal load` `, parts` EMPTY
                `, paint` NOTHING `, police suspension` TRUE `, earlier part thefts` 0

#TRACE `5.2.10 — the purchaser reports a theft of the vehicle within 24 hours` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the purchaser` DOES `notify the police and the insurer of the theft` AT 20
#ASSERT `the amount payable on` `a stolen car reported after 20 hours` EQUALS 522_000_000

§§ `X4 — double insurance and under-insurance stack`

-- Two contracts of 300m each on a car worth 600m: together exactly the value, which is not
-- double insurance under Article 49(1) of the Law. The Rules pro-rate twice: 16.5m x 0.5 -
-- 0.5m = 7.75m, then this insurer's half of that, 3.875m. Two such insurers pay 7.75m of a
-- 16.5m loss.
`a loss under one of two half insurances` MEANS
    `a claim: vehicle` `the standard vehicle` `, policy` (`a 2026 policy with sum insured` 300_000_000 `, deductible` NOTHING `, clauses` EMPTY)
        `, claimant` `the insured named on the certificate` `, event` `the standard collision` `, driving` `the standard driving` `, conduct` `prompt and proper conduct`
        `, shortfall` `no premium shortfall` `, costs` `no costs` `, hire` NOTHING `, wreck` `no wreck kept`
        `, other insurance` (LIST (`Another insurance of the vehicle` WITH `the sum insured under it` IS 300_000_000, `on the same conditions as this contract` IS TRUE))

#ASSERT `the amount payable on` `a loss under one of two half insurances` EQUALS 3_875_000

§§ `X5 — 7.1.2(d) and 11.2 have different exceptions`

-- A vehicle circulating temporarily with the authority's approval, damaged on 15 June with no
-- inspection certificate: 7.1.2(d) does not ask for the certificate, and 11.2 excludes the loss.
`a temporarily circulating vehicle damaged without an inspection certificate` MEANS
    `a standard claim for` `the event`
    WHERE
        `the event` MEANS
            `an event on` (YMD 2026 6 15) `: peril` `a collision` `, sudden` TRUE `, at` `in Vietnam` `, war` FALSE `, deliberate` EMPTY
                `, hired out` FALSE `, inspection` (`inspection: valid` FALSE `, new and awaiting inspection` FALSE `, circulating temporarily` TRUE) `, load` `a normal load` `, parts` `the standard parts`
                `, paint` NOTHING `, police suspension` FALSE `, earlier part thefts` 0

`the same vehicle's circumstances` MEANS `The circumstances of the claim` WITH
    `the police took part in dealing with the accident`         IS FALSE
    `a third party is liable for the damage`                    IS FALSE
    `settled by mediation`                                      IS FALSE
    `a court judgment or decision`                              IS FALSE
    `the vehicle was sold, transferred, given or lent`          IS FALSE
    `the vehicle was stolen or robbed whole`                    IS FALSE
    `a criminal case was opened`                                IS FALSE
    `papers kept in the stolen vehicle were lost with it`       IS FALSE
    `circulating temporarily with the written approval of the competent authority` IS TRUE
    `in the course of its first registration and inspection in Vietnam` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT elem `7.1.2(d) a valid inspection certificate` (`Article 7 — the documents the claim file may contain, for` `the same vehicle's circumstances`)
#ASSERT `the cover decision for` `a temporarily circulating vehicle damaged without an inspection certificate` EQUALS `excluded by` (LIST `11.2 no valid inspection certificate`)

§§ `X8 — one notice of a change in risk, two clocks of "5 days"`

-- A notice received on Thursday 8 October 2026: the answer to a request to reduce the premium
-- is due in 5 days (13 October), the re-rating in 5 working days (15 October).
#ASSERT `5.2.4(a) — the last day for the insurer to answer a request to reduce the premium` (YMD 2026 10 8) EQUALS YMD 2026 10 13
#ASSERT `4.2.7 — the last day to reassess the risk after a notice received on` (YMD 2026 10 8) `, the public holidays being` EMPTY EQUALS YMD 2026 10 15

§§ `X9 and X10 — the premium and the purchaser`

`unpaid, payment agreed by 31 January (X10)` MEANS
    `premium arrangements: written agreement` TRUE `, due` (YMD 2026 1 31) `, paid in full on` NOTHING `, continued from` NOTHING
`a purchaser who has agreed to pay later` MEANS `The purchaser` WITH
    `owns the vehicle`                                                     IS TRUE
    `holds or uses the vehicle lawfully, the owner having handed it over`  IS FALSE
    `concluded the contract with the insurer`                              IS TRUE
    `paid the premium in full`                                             IS FALSE

-- X10: the contract is in effect on 20 January under 2.2's written agreement, yet the person
-- who concluded it is not "the purchaser" of definition 2, which requires full payment.
#ASSERT `the standing on` (YMD 2026 1 20) `as to the premium under` `unpaid, payment agreed by 31 January (X10)` EQUALS `in effect`
#ASSERT NOT `a purchaser within definition 2` `a purchaser who has agreed to pay later`

§§ `X16 — BVVC05 read literally caps the whole benefit at one day's sum insured`

-- The alternative reading, written out only to show what it gives; the encoding takes the
-- per-day reading (fork F38). Ten days at 1m, 800,000 a day, 8m an event.
GIVEN `the costs`  IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `per day`    IS A NUMBER
      `per event`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Article 20 read literally: the benefit for` `the costs` `, per day` `per day` `, per event` `per event` MEANS
    min `per day` (min `per event` (max 0 (sum `the costs` MINUS 3 TIMES `per day`)))

#ASSERT `Article 20 read literally: the benefit for` (replicate 10 1_000_000) `, per day` 800_000 `, per event` 8_000_000 EQUALS 800_000
#ASSERT `Article 20 — the benefit for daily costs` (replicate 10 1_000_000) `, per day` 800_000 `, per event` 8_000_000 `, reduced by` 0 EQUALS 5_600_000

§§ `X17 — no force-majeure exception to the 6-hour rule`

-- Force majeure excuses late WRITTEN notice (15.1.1(b)) but not a late call (15.1.1(a)):
-- told after 10 hours, force majeure or not, 10% off. LAW: Articles 19(3) and 46(1) of the Law.
#ASSERT `the amount payable on` (`the standard collision, with conduct` (`conduct: told after hours` (JUST 10) `, written notice after days` (JUST 2) `, force majeure` TRUE `, moved without consent` FALSE `, for safety` FALSE `, repaired without consent` FALSE `, dishonest` FALSE `, 15.1.3 rate` NOTHING)) EQUALS 14_350_000

§§ `X20 — BVVC06 pays the sum insured on a total loss, above the market value at the loss`

GIVEN `the clauses` IS A LIST OF `A supplementary clause`
GIVETH A `A claim`
`a total loss at value, under clauses` `the clauses` MEANS
    `a standard claim under` (`the standard policy with` `the clauses`) `for` `the event` `,` `the standard driving`
    WHERE
        `the event` MEANS
            `a sudden` `a collision` `on 15 June 2026, damaging` (LIST (`a part replaced:` "engine" `, of kind` `the engine` `, caused by` `the insured event itself` `, for` 600_000_000))

-- Market value at the loss 580m, sum insured 600m: 580m without BVVC06, 600m with it.
#ASSERT `the amount payable on` (`a total loss at value, under clauses` EMPTY) EQUALS 580_000_000
#ASSERT `the amount payable on` (`a total loss at value, under clauses` (LIST `BVVC06 (settlement up to the limit of liability)`)) EQUALS 600_000_000

§§ `X23 — a notice of termination may name a date already past`

`the standard policy, with an insurer's notice of 20 June naming 1 June` MEANS
    `a 2026 policy: sum insured` 600_000_000 `, deductible` NOTHING `, clauses` EMPTY `, ending` (YMD 2026 12 31)
        `, premium` `premium paid in full at conclusion` `, notice` (JUST `the notice`) `, transfer` NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the notice` MEANS
            `A notice of unilateral termination` WITH
                `given by`                         IS `the insurer`
                `date of the notice`               IS YMD 2026 6 20
                `the termination date it states`   IS JUST (YMD 2026 6 1)
                `date the other party received it` IS YMD 2026 6 22

#ASSERT `the cover decision for` (`a standard claim under` `the standard policy, with an insurer's notice of 20 June naming 1 June` `for` `the standard collision` `,` `the standard driving`) EQUALS `the contract was not in effect` `ended by a notice of unilateral termination (3.2.1)`

§§ `X24 — a change in risk is penalised inside the time allowed to report it`

-- The car is converted on Wednesday 10 June 2026; 5.2.4 allows until 1 July (15 working days)
-- to report it. The loss on 15 June is inside that time, yet 15.1.5(b) scales the compensation
-- by premium paid over premium due: 3.65m of 4.38m, so 16.5m x 5/6 - 0.5m = 13.25m.
#ASSERT `5.2.4 — the last day to notify a change in risk made on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `, the public holidays being` EMPTY EQUALS YMD 2026 7 1
#ASSERT `the amount payable on` (`a claim: vehicle` `the standard vehicle` `, policy` `the standard policy` `, claimant` `the insured named on the certificate` `, event` `the standard collision` `, driving` `the standard driving` `, conduct` `prompt and proper conduct` `, shortfall` (`a shortfall: misdeclared` FALSE `, risk increase not told` TRUE `, paid` 3_650_000 `, due` (JUST 4_380_000)) `, costs` `no costs` `, hire` NOTHING `, wreck` `no wreck kept` `, other insurance` EMPTY) EQUALS 13_250_000
